This codebase is for an online adaption of the card game 7th Sea: City of Five Sails. Specifically this code is written to run on the Board Game Arena framework. 

Anything related to the backend is written in PHP.  
Anything written for the UI or front-end is written in Javascript.  jQuery is available. Dojo is available.

The entire backend is a state machine and centers around the file:states.inc.php.  states.inc.php is a huge associative array.  The indexes for the array are named constants.  
states.inc.php also includes the file states.7s5s.php which includes the same function.
There are three types of states:
1. game: This is a state run by the state machine automatically when the state is transitioned to.  There is no player interaction with this state.
2. activeplayer: This is a single-player state.  The game waits for the player to perform an action and then transitions to another state based on the action.
3. multipleactiveplayer: This is a multi-player state.  The game waits for all players to perform an action, then transitions to antoher state.

Each state in the game is an array element in states.inc.php.  Each element describes the state.

Each element contains an associative array as follows:
1. "name" => The human-readable name of the state, used as a reference in many javascript methods
2. "type" => The statetype: game, activeplayer, or multipleactiveplayer
3. "args" => if statetype=activeplayer or statetype=multipleactiveplayer, the name of the PHP function that will supply arguments to the Ajax return on the Javascript-side.  The function will return an associatetive array.
4. "possibleactions" => An array of strings containing the names of the PHP methods that could be called from the Javascript-side when a player submits an action.
5. "action" => If statetype=multipleactiveplayer, the name of the PHP function that will be called when all players have submitted their action. If statetype=game, the name of the PHP function that auto-runs when the state is transitioned to.
6. "transitions" => An associative array of named transitions to other states.